# release workflow scratch (assembled launcher kits — CI artifacts, never committed)
/release/

# ROUND-51 (R51-a): staged sidecar bundle for the NSIS installer (CI assembles
# it via scripts/release/stage-sidecar.mjs + the pinned node.exe — never committed)
# ROUND-57: the old three-line form un-ignored the sidecar/ DIRECTORY itself,
# which re-includes EVERYTHING inside it — a local staging run + `git add -A`
# would sweep 124 MB of node_modules into the index (caught before commit).
# The correct form ignores the CONTENTS of sidecar/ and re-includes only the
# README placeholder that tauri-build needs on fresh checkouts.
/src-tauri/staging/*
/src-tauri/staging/sidecar/*
!/src-tauri/staging/sidecar/README.md

# ROUND-100 (R100-A): the fixedRuntime bundle is RETIRED — the installer
# returned to the evergreen downloadBootstrapper (~37–40 MB) and the
# webview2-runtime staging dir + CI fetch are gone. Nothing to ignore anymore.

# tooling caches
.vite/
.turbo/
coverage/
.dev
.runner-bin/
acute-runner.log.old
__pycache__/

# ROUND-106 (R106-S4a): the Android companion — mobile/ is a STANDALONE npm
# workspace outside pnpm-workspace.yaml (own lockfile, ANDROID-R3 §2). Its
# generated native shells and tool caches are never committed: CI prebuilds
# and builds them fresh per run (the android-apk job), so only the source
# (app/, src/, modules/, app.json, lockfile) lives in the repo.
/mobile/android/
/mobile/ios/
/mobile/.expo/
/mobile/web-build/
